{{draft}}
'''{{Ill|{{PAGENAME}}|ja|海神神社|simple}}''' (海神神社) is a significant Shinto shrine located in [[Tsushima Island]], Nagasaki that holds a [[Beppyo shrine|Beppyo status]]. This status denotes that the shrine is remarkable and holds a significant historical importance. Kaijin Shrine is also ranked as an [[Ichinomiya]], which means it is the highest-ranked shrine in its province.

Kaijin Shrine should not be confused with {{Ill|Watatsumi jinja|lt=Watatsumi Shrine|simple}}, which has a very similar Japanese name (海神社) to Kaijin Shrine (海神神社).

In 2012 a robber stole a Buddha statue from the shrine, but in 2015 it was returned.<ref>{{Cite web |title=South Korea Returns Stolen Buddhist Statue to Japan {{!}} Buddhistdoor |url=https://www2.buddhistdoor.net/news/south-korea-returns-stolen-buddhist-statue-to-japan |access-date=2023-04-25 |website=www2.buddhistdoor.net}}</ref>

