In 2012 a robber stole a Silla era Buddha statue from the shrine<ref name=":0" />, on the same day they stole another statue from [[Kannon-ji (Tokushima)|Kannon-ji]]<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hae-yeon |first=Kim |date=2023-10-26 |title=Supreme Court dismisses Buseoksa's appeal in Bodhisattva statue ownership dispute |url=https://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20231026000667 |access-date=2023-10-27 |website=The Korea Herald |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hae-yeon |first=Kim |date=2023-02-06 |title=Buseoksa to appeal court ruling on Bodhisattva statue stolen from Japan |url=https://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20230206000649 |access-date=2023-10-27 |website=The Korea Herald |language=en}}</ref> but in 2015 it was returned.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=South Korea Returns Stolen Buddhist Statue to Japan {{!}} Buddhistdoor |url=https://www2.buddhistdoor.net/news/south-korea-returns-stolen-buddhist-statue-to-japan |access-date=2023-04-25 |website=www2.buddhistdoor.net}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Press |first=Jiji |date=2023-02-02 |title=S. Korean Court Denies Temple’s Ownership of Statue Stolen from Japan |url=https://japannews.yomiuri.co.jp/society/general-news/20230202-88365/ |access-date=2023-10-27 |website=japannews.yomiuri.co.jp |language=en}}</ref>

