In 2012 a robber stole a Silla era Buddha statue from the shrine<ref name="www2buddhistdoornet-2023a" />, on the same day they stole another statue from [[Kannon-ji]]<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hae-yeon |first=Kim |date=2023-10-26 |title=Supreme Court dismisses Buseoksa's appeal in Bodhisattva statue ownership dispute |url=https://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20231026000667 |access-date=2023-10-27 |website=The Korea Herald |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hae-yeon |first=Kim |date=2023-02-06 |title=Buseoksa to appeal court ruling on Bodhisattva statue stolen from Japan |url=https://www.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=20230206000649 |access-date=2023-10-27 |website=The Korea Herald |language=en}}</ref> but in 2015 it was returned.<ref name="www2buddhistdoornet-2023a">{{Cite web |title=South Korea Returns Stolen Buddhist Statue to Japan {{!}} Buddhistdoor |url=https://www2.buddhistdoor.net/news/south-korea-returns-stolen-buddhist-statue-to-japan |access-date=2023-04-25 |website=www2.buddhistdoor.net}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Press |first=Jiji |date=2023-02-02 |title=S. Korean Court Denies Temple's Ownership of Statue Stolen from Japan |url=https://japannews.yomiuri.co.jp/society/general-news/20230202-88365/ |access-date=2023-10-27 |website=japannews.yomiuri.co.jp |language=en}}</ref>
[[Ghost of Tsushima]] fans helped raise money to repair it.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-01-12 |title=Ghost of Tsushima fans come together to help fund repair of Watatsumi Shrine gate |url=https://www.destructoid.com/ghost-of-tsushima-fans-come-together-to-help-fund-repair-of-watatsumi-shrine-gate/ |access-date=2023-10-27 |website=Destructoid |language=en-US}}</ref>
