In January 2020 they banned foreigners due to behavioral issues by [[South Korea|South Korean]] guests.<ref name=":8">{{Cite web |date=2020-01-14 |title=Japan’s Watatsumi Shrine bans foreigners after vandalism and alleged death threat against priest {{!}} South China Morning Post |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200114080417/https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3046010/japans-watatsumi-shrine-bans-foreigners-after-vandalism-and |access-date=2023-11-20 |website=web.archive.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Wen |first=Lok Jian |date=2023-07-10 |title=Vandalism, peeling ceiling art: Japan temples suffer damage |language=en |work=The Straits Times |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/asia/east-asia/vandalism-peeling-ceiling-art-japan-temples-suffer-damage-to-tourist-sites#:~:text=In%20western%20Japan's%20Nagasaki%20prefecture,language%20and%20theft%20of%20amulets. |access-date=2023-11-20 |issn=0585-3923}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2020-01-13 |title=Japanese shrine bans foreign visitors following disrespectful behaviour by tourists |url=https://soranews24.com/2020/01/13/japanese-shrine-bans-foreign-visitors-following-disrespectful-behaviour-by-tourists/ |access-date=2023-11-20 |website=SoraNews24 -Japan News- |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Alyse |date=2023-02-09 |title=Overtourism in Japan: A Victim of its Own Success? |url=https://www.theinvisibletourist.com/overtourism-in-japan-tourist-pollution/ |access-date=2023-11-20 |website=The Invisible Tourist |language=en-AU}}</ref>
